Stopping at the relay boundary. Summary of this session's work:

**Corrected the campaign map for defect #1.** The ledger's `next` field for D-FOREIGN-REPLAY-UNGATED-IMAGES is stale — it points at "step 2 residue / step 3" of the sess197 tenure-release build order, but code inspection proved steps 1-4 are all landed (step 3 release-state machine in sess200/201, step 4 F4 obligation registry in sess227 at 0.11.481, telemetry mode). The campaign paused there while sessions 228-252 worked other defects. The true next step is **build-order step 5: F3 — completion-driven release proof, ICLUS into common accounting, kill the relbar fast path unless flush-ticketed**. F1/F3/F4 readiness constants are all still 0 (`xfs_mxfs_dlm.c:39574-39576`).

**Found a live soundness hole while reading the ICLUS path.** `mxfs_iclus_make_durable` treats a TRYLOCK failure on the cluster buffer as "settled", with a comment claiming the subsequent flush covers a submitted write's durability — but a device flush does not cover a bio still in flight, so a prior-tenure inode-cluster write can land after the peer's cold read (the same mechanism as the proven dir_reuse readdir=799 loss, which is why the P3B bio counter exists for dir buffers). Inode-cluster writes are counted nowhere today.

**RULE-5 consult done, ruling recorded.** GPT reviewed my step-5 design and amended it in three load-bearing ways: (A) the ICLUS release wait must be keyed by cluster daddr (a per-cluster registry with inflight + submit/complete generations, entries kept until unmount so generations can't alias), never the device-wide aggregate; (B) the proof needs a generation check across the flush, since a dirty-recheck misses a full submit+complete cycle landing in the target cache after the flush; (E) F3_COMPLETION_PROOF_READY stays 0 until step 6 makes proof failures release-blocking. Ruling saved to ccmemory (`ccloop-c7ee71c6-sess253-GPT-ruling-step5-F3-iclus-ticket-shape`) and a full implementation inventory — six file-level work items with line anchors — is in `.ccloop/handoff.md`. No code was written this session; the next session implements the inventory, builds 0.11.490, and boards it.

Criteria not met: 34 defects remain open in the RULE 6 ledger (23 critical), so MXFS is not production ready. The loop continues in the next session.

